From 7fae9b1be633fd857e66fca59a17b2764dceca0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abdelhafid DJIDEL <266947999+hafid-logic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:51:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(fs-policy): pin ObjectId availability to either nonzero
 component

### What
Pins `ObjectId::is_available`: an object is available iff `device != 0` OR `inode != 0`. The test covers `(0,0)` unavailable and `(7,0)`, `(0,7)`, `(7,9)` available.

### Why it matters
Availability gates object identity. The existing tests do not exercise `is_available` directly, so a fault that requires both components nonzero (or inverts the device check) survives them.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| `device != 0` -> `== 0` | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| `||` -> `&&` | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline (clean tree + new test): PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-fs-policy --lib object_id`.

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-fs-policy/src/lib.rs | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-fs-policy/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-fs-policy/src/lib.rs
index e4151e4..c38f04e 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-fs-policy/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-fs-policy/src/lib.rs
@@ -1981,4 +1981,29 @@ mod tests {
         assert!(!Rights::READ.contains(need));
         assert!(!Rights(0).contains(Rights::LOOKUP));
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn object_id_available_when_either_component_nonzero() {
+        assert!(!ObjectId::UNAVAILABLE.is_available());
+        assert!(!ObjectId {
+            device: 0,
+            inode: 0
+        }
+        .is_available());
+        assert!(ObjectId {
+            device: 7,
+            inode: 0
+        }
+        .is_available());
+        assert!(ObjectId {
+            device: 0,
+            inode: 7
+        }
+        .is_available());
+        assert!(ObjectId {
+            device: 7,
+            inode: 9
+        }
+        .is_available());
+    }
 }
